From 4a111a2f66b16f1650a479156fcf72417a3df98b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 3dpdf <3dpdf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:52:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip re-applying an identical transform one hop back in a
 prototype chain

prc_api_helper_add_product follows PRC "prototype" (shared part
definition) references by walking occurrence -> prototype -> ... in
place, composing each hop's own has_transform matrix via
prc_api_update_transform. Reproduced against a real multi-part
assembly PDF: for several components, the occurrence's own transform
and its resolved prototype's own transform decoded to byte-identical
matrices, and composing both doubled the effective placement (verified
numerically -- the composed translation was exactly 2x a single
application's value on two independent axes).

Track the last-applied transform per chain and skip composing a hop's
transform when it exactly matches the one just applied one hop back.
This only changes behavior for literal duplicates, so a legitimate
multi-level chain where each hop's transform genuinely differs still
composes every hop as before.

Verified against a real 4-part assembly PDF (enclosure + 2 PCBs + an
interposer connector): before this change, several components rendered
detached from the assembly; after, isolating each top-level part and
checking it against the enclosure individually shows the larger PCB
seated near the top (parallel to the floor), the smaller PCB seated
against the bottom, and the interposer connector near the larger
board's header -- matching the assembly's known correct layout. One
smaller residual offset remains in a sub-feature of the interposer
part (unclear cause, much smaller magnitude, not visually obvious).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/prc_api.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/prc_api.c b/src/prc_api.c
index 2b2ab23..99a6a3b 100644
--- a/src/prc_api.c
+++ b/src/prc_api.c
@@ -3286,6 +3286,8 @@ prc_api_helper_add_product(prc_context *ctx, prc_api_data data, uint32_t num_fil
         uint32_t work_parent_biased_style_file_index = item.parent_biased_style_file_index;
         prc_api_product *work_product_tree = item.product_tree;
         prc_api_object_style *work_parent_style = item.parent_style;
+        prc_api_transform chain_last_applied;
+        uint8_t chain_has_last_applied = 0;
 
         for (;;)
         {
@@ -3369,7 +3371,18 @@ prc_api_helper_add_product(prc_context *ctx, prc_api_data data, uint32_t num_fil
                     result = code;
                     goto cleanup;
                 }
-                prc_api_update_transform(ctx, &work_incoming_transform, &new_transform);
+                /* Skip composing this transform if it is byte-identical to
+                   the one just applied one hop back in this same prototype
+                   chain -- avoids double-applying what appears to be a single
+                   placement redundantly stored at both the occurrence and its
+                   prototype for some files. */
+                if (!(chain_has_last_applied &&
+                      memcmp(&new_transform, &chain_last_applied, sizeof(prc_api_transform)) == 0))
+                {
+                    prc_api_update_transform(ctx, &work_incoming_transform, &new_transform);
+                }
+                chain_last_applied = new_transform;
+                chain_has_last_applied = 1;
             }
 
             /* !(wants_cross_file_ref && biased_file_index == 0): don't follow
-- 
